# Source is edited from multiple platforms; store and check out LF so that a
# Windows editor cannot silently rewrite an entire file's line endings and bury
# a real change in a whole-file diff.
#
# Deliberately scoped to src/ and test/ rather than `*`: several tracked text
# files still have CRLF blobs in the index (package.json, package-lock.json,
# README.md, .gitignore, demo/data/*.csv, demo/lib/sylvester.js). A repo-wide
# rule would renormalize each of those the next time it is touched -- e.g.
# `npm version` would rewrite every line of package.json. Widening this to `*`
# is the right long-term fix, but it should land as its own commit alongside
# `git add --renormalize .` so the churn is intentional and reviewable.
src/**   text eol=lf
test/**  text eol=lf
